  "Question": "Which of the following is always a valid square root expression?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\sqrt{-2}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\sqrt{a-1}\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Since \\(x^2+1\\ge1>0\\), \\(\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\) is always defined. The expression \\(\\sqrt{-2}\\) is undefined, \\(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\) is a cube root expression, and \\(\\sqrt{a-1}\\) is undefined when \\(a<1\\).",
